"""Preparation reference for ``_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward`` (out-of-place).

Injected through the project's formal ``--override`` entry for the
``reference-as-solution`` probe, i.e. ``flag_gems._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward``
is temporarily bound to this module's ``run`` (see
``flag_gems.dynamic_registry.DynamicOpOverride.override_from_file``).

The frozen test's own oracle is
``torch.ops.aten._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.default(grad_output,
output_size, input_size, *scales)``, so the wrapper forwards exactly that call.
It deliberately does not import or call ``flag_gems``: the candidate export must
not be its own oracle, and this keeps the observed chain
``test -> flag_gems._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward -> run -> native ATen``
free of recursion through the replaced module attribute.

ABI accepted here is the candidate-side ABI used by both suites:

* ``tests/test_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.py`` calls
  ``flag_gems._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward(grad_output, output_size,
  input_size, *scales)`` (six positional arguments, ``scales`` may be
  ``(None, None, None)``).
* ``benchmark/test_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.py`` yields
  ``grad_output, output_size, input_size, *scales`` and the runner calls the
  injected callable with those positional arguments.

Semantics kept identical to the frozen Definition
(``definitions/_upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward.json``): a fresh output
tensor of shape ``input_size`` with the dtype/device of ``grad_output``; the
operator mutates no argument and returns no alias (``mutates: []``,
``returns_alias_of: {}``). No tolerance, dtype or device handling is added or
relaxed here - comparisons stay in the frozen test helpers.
"""

import torch

# Resolved at call time so the wrapper always uses the live ATen overload the
# frozen test also uses as its reference; no FlagGems export is touched.
_ATEN_BACKWARD = torch.ops.aten._upsample_nearest_exact3d_backward


def run(
    grad_output,
    output_size,
    input_size,
    scales_d=None,
    scales_h=None,
    scales_w=None,
):
    """Return the native exact-nearest 3d backward result for ``grad_output``."""
    return _ATEN_BACKWARD.default(
        grad_output,
        output_size,
        input_size,
        scales_d,
        scales_h,
        scales_w,
    )
